Summary of modifications (each derived file lists its own in its header):
- Reconstructed as strict TypeScript from the compiled JavaScript and type
  declarations of 0.0.72 (no TypeScript source of that version is published);
  function names, file split and AST node shapes are kept.
- The event-emitter dependency (core/runtime/async/event-emitter) is removed;
  comments are collected in an array on the parser, each comment once.
- Tokens are matched with sticky regular expressions compiled once instead of
  exec() on input.substr(loc); keywords require a word boundary; the global
  per-accept loop counter is replaced by progress checks; the linear
  offsetToColRow / getAroundText helpers are removed (see position.ts).
- Comment attachment (leading / trailing / detached groups) re-implemented
  after protoc's tokenizer and parser rules; block statements take their
  trailing comment after "{" instead of after "}".
- Grammar extensions: edition 2024 "export" / "local" visibility on messages
  and enums, "import option", identifiers in "reserved", options on oneof
  groups, "\u" / "\U" string escapes, hexadecimal values in text-format
  aggregates, "map" and "stream" usable as type names, dotted option names
  mixing plain and parenthesised segments split into separate segments.
- Error handling: parsing never throws; a syntax error (including pbkit's
  recovered "malformed-field" and trailing input) is returned with the offset
  of the unexpected token and an empty AST.
